   "section": "SERVER — WEBSOCKET HANDSHAKE (once per connection)",
   "role": {
    "title": "accept()",
    "text": "The only await/yield point in the whole handshake, and it now runs first — unconditionally, before any check. A real ASGI server discards a close code sent before accept() (a bare HTTP 403 instead), which is why this must come before the checks below rather than after.",
    "file": "backend/chat_router.py — room_socket()"
   }
  },
  {
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
