   "x": 90,
   "y": 624,
   "width": 640,
   "height": 98,
   "section": "SERVER — WEBSOCKET HANDSHAKE (once per connection)",
   "role": {
    "title": "Why accept() is first",
    "text": "A real ASGI server (uvicorn) silently discards a close code sent before accept(), returning a bare HTTP 403 instead — invisible against Starlette's TestClient, which preserves it faithfully. Accepting first also retires the old post-register re-check: there's no yield point left between the membership check and registration for anything to interleave in.",
    "file": "backend/chat_router.py (see its docstring); README.md — Two testing gotchas, #1"
   }
  },
  {
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1272882936,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1779835050,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1784619688305,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "type": "text",
   "id": "h5_txt",
   "x": 146,
   "y": 631.5,
   "width": 528,
   "height": 83,
   "text": "Why accept() is first:\nreal uvicorn discards a close code sent BEFORE accept() —\nthe client just sees a bare HTTP 403.\nTestClient has no such limit — this only shows up against a real server.\nOne check, right after accept(), is now enough —\nit's the only yield point, already before the checks, so nothing can interleave.",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "h5",
   "originalText": "Why accept() is first:\nreal uvicorn discards a close code sent BEFORE accept() —\nthe client just sees a bare HTTP 403.\nTestClient has no such limit — this only shows up against a real server.\nOne check, right after accept(), is now enough —\nit's the only yield point, already before the checks, so nothing can interleave.",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "baseline": 11
  },
  {
