   "section": "⚠ TESTING GOTCHAS (two of them)",
   "role": {
    "title": "Two testing gotchas",
    "text": "Both are a test double disagreeing with the real ASGI server, in opposite directions. (1) TestClient is MORE permissive pre-accept — it preserves a close code sent before accept() that a real server discards, masking the HTTP-403 bug. (2) TestClient is LESS permissive on event loops — each simulated connection gets its own, so broadcasting between two connections open in one test hangs unless you share a portal.",
    "file": "README.md — 'Two testing gotchas'"
   }
  },
