   "id": "g1_txt",
   "x": 146,
   "y": 1181.5,
   "width": 968,
   "height": 49,
   "text": "If your test harness gives each simulated WebSocket connection its OWN event loop (e.g. Starlette's TestClient, by default),\nbroadcasting between two connections open in ONE test hangs forever — a cross-event-loop await. Fix: share one event\nloop/portal per test client. Production never hits this: one process serves every connection on one loop.",
